// Structural signatures: what each concept IS, stripped of the vocabulary of its
// field. The rule is strict — no word that names the domain may appear. Not
// "plants", "money", "genes", "notes": only mechanism, driver, constraint, and
// failure mode.
//
// The point: two concepts that describe the same underlying structure share
// almost no words in their DEFINITIONS (which is why definition embeddings put
// them far apart) but share most of their words HERE. Embedding these instead
// turns "far apart but analogous" into "near", which is a far easier retrieval
// problem than searching a distant tail.
//
// Written by an LLM against a fixed template, which is exactly how this scales:
// see scripts/generate_structures.py.
{"id": "photosynthesis", "structure": "A system captures a diffuse ambient flux and locks it into a concentrated recoverable store through a catalytic cycle. Throughput is set by the scarcest required input. Fails when the capture apparatus saturates."}
{"id": "natural-selection", "structure": "Variation is generated blindly, filtered by differential retention, and the surviving set biases the next round. Driven by a success signal nobody computes deliberately. Fails when the filter shifts faster than the population can track."}
{"id": "homeostasis", "structure": "A controller compares a measured state against a target and applies opposing correction. Driven by deviation from a set point. Fails when disturbance exceeds the correction range."}
{"id": "apoptosis", "structure": "Damaged or surplus components are removed on an internal signal so the larger whole is preserved. Limited by the accuracy of damage detection. Fails when the removal signal is suppressed, or fires on healthy parts."}
{"id": "symbiosis", "structure": "Two distinct systems couple so each supplies what the other cannot produce, stabilising both. Driven by complementary deficits. Fails when one side can withdraw its contribution without penalty."}
{"id": "gene-expression", "structure": "A stored instruction is selectively read and converted into an active working form on demand. Driven by regulatory gates on access. Fails when the gating is bypassed or the read is corrupted."}
{"id": "immune-memory", "structure": "A costly first response is stored so a repeat of the same input is answered far faster. Keyed on a retained signature. Fails when the input drifts past the stored key."}
{"id": "metamorphosis", "structure": "A system passes through a destructive intermediate in which its organisation is dismantled and rebuilt to a different plan. Carried by reserves banked before the transition. Fails catastrophically if interrupted midway."}
{"id": "circadian-rhythm", "structure": "An internal oscillator free-runs at an approximate period and is pulled into phase by an external periodic cue. Limited by entrainment range. Fails when the external cue conflicts with the internal phase."}
{"id": "horizontal-gene-transfer", "structure": "A working component is copied sideways between unrelated systems instead of inherited down a lineage. Driven by contact and exchange. Fails when the receiving system cannot integrate the imported part."}
{"id": "entropy", "structure": "A count of how many indistinguishable fine arrangements match one coarse description, which grows whenever constraints are released. Driven by the overwhelming numerical dominance of disordered configurations. Misleads when the system is far from settled."}
{"id": "phase-transition", "structure": "Continuous change in a control parameter produces almost no effect until a threshold, at which the bulk organisation reorganises abruptly. Driven by competition between two tendencies. Blurs in small or heterogeneous systems."}
{"id": "resonance", "structure": "Periodic driving matched to a system's own natural rate accumulates instead of cancelling, producing a disproportionate response. Driven by phase alignment between forcing and response. Limited by dissipation."}
{"id": "conservation-of-energy", "structure": "A quantity that can be moved and transformed without limit but never created or destroyed inside a closed boundary. Constrains every accounting of what a process can do. Fails as bookkeeping when the boundary leaks."}
{"id": "quantum-entanglement", "structure": "Two parts of a system share a joint description that cannot be factored into independent descriptions of each. Correlation is fixed at preparation, not transmitted afterwards. Destroyed by uncontrolled interaction with the surroundings."}
{"id": "symmetry-breaking", "structure": "A system whose governing rules are indifferent between options settles into one specific option, so the outcome is less symmetric than the law producing it. Driven by instability of the symmetric state. The choice is arbitrary but then locked in."}
{"id": "critical-mass", "structure": "Below a threshold quantity a process dies out; above it, each event triggers more than one successor and the process becomes self-sustaining. Driven by a per-event replacement ratio crossing one. Sensitive to geometry and losses at the boundary."}
{"id": "diffusion", "structure": "Random independent movement of many units produces a reliable net drift from crowded regions toward empty ones, with no coordination and no directed force. Rate falls off sharply with distance. Slow over long ranges."}
{"id": "hysteresis", "structure": "The present state depends on the path of past inputs, not only on the current input, so the system does not retrace itself when the input reverses. Driven by internal states that resist switching. Produces lag and stuck configurations."}
{"id": "event-horizon", "structure": "A boundary past which information can travel inward but never back out, so what lies beyond is unobservable in principle rather than merely unmeasured. Defined by escape being impossible, not merely hard."}
{"id": "catalysis", "structure": "An agent lowers the barrier to a transformation and is returned unchanged, so a small persistent quantity enables an unlimited amount of change. Limited by the agent being blocked or degraded. Changes rate, never the destination."}
{"id": "chemical-equilibrium", "structure": "Two opposing processes run at equal rates, so the visible composition stops changing while both continue underneath. Driven by rates converging, not by activity ceasing. Shifts when any participant is added or removed."}
{"id": "polymerisation", "structure": "Small identical units join into long chains whose bulk properties bear no resemblance to the properties of the unit. Driven by repeated identical linking. Reversing it requires breaking every link."}
{"id": "solubility", "structure": "The extent to which one substance can be dispersed uniformly into another before the mixture saturates and further additions separate out. Set by compatibility of the two. Has a hard ceiling."}
{"id": "chirality", "structure": "A structure not superimposable on its mirror image, so two forms are identical in every internal measure yet behave differently when they meet another handed structure. Difference appears only on interaction."}
{"id": "activation-energy", "structure": "A barrier that must be climbed before a transition that is favourable overall can begin, so a beneficial change does not happen spontaneously. Sets the rate, not the outcome. Lowered by anything that reduces the barrier."}
{"id": "recursion", "structure": "A thing is defined by reference to smaller instances of itself, so an unbounded structure is specified in finite terms. Requires a base case that terminates. Fails by never bottoming out."}
{"id": "isomorphism", "structure": "A correspondence that preserves all relevant structure, so two systems that look unrelated are the same system in different clothing. Anything proved in one transfers to the other. Fails when the correspondence misses a relevant relation."}
{"id": "fixed-point", "structure": "A configuration left unchanged by the transformation applied to it, so repeated application settles there and stops. Attracts nearby states when stable, repels them when not."}
{"id": "topology", "structure": "The study of what survives continuous deformation, so properties that persist under stretching are separated from those that depend on exact measurement. Ignores size and shape, keeps connection."}
{"id": "combinatorial-explosion", "structure": "The number of possibilities grows multiplicatively with problem size, so exhaustive approaches that work at small scale become impossible at slightly larger scale. Defeats brute force abruptly, not gradually."}
{"id": "duality", "structure": "Every statement in one system has a mirror statement in another, so a hard question can be exchanged for an easier equivalent one. Requires the correspondence to be exact. Value is in choosing which side to work on."}
{"id": "invariant", "structure": "A quantity that stays fixed while everything else about a system changes, so it can be used to rule out transitions that would alter it. Proves impossibility cheaply. Useless if it does not actually hold."}
{"id": "gradient-descent", "structure": "Repeatedly take a small step in whichever direction locally improves an objective, using only local information and no global view. Driven by a measurable slope. Gets stuck in local optima and stalls where the slope is flat."}
{"id": "phase-space", "structure": "An abstract space in which every possible complete state of a system is a single point, so the system's history becomes a path and its tendencies become geometry. Turns dynamics into shape."}
{"id": "incompleteness", "structure": "Any system powerful enough to describe itself contains true statements it cannot establish from within, so self-reference sets a ceiling that no amount of added effort inside the system removes. The limit is structural, not practical."}
{"id": "regression-to-the-mean", "structure": "When an outcome mixes a stable component with noise, extreme observations were partly luck, so the next observation is closer to typical regardless of any intervention. Fools anyone who intervenes after an extreme and credits the result."}
{"id": "overfitting", "structure": "A model committed so tightly to the specific sample it was shown that it captures the sample's accidents as if they were the underlying pattern, and performs worse on anything new. Driven by capacity exceeding evidence."}
{"id": "base-rate-neglect", "structure": "Vivid specific evidence is weighted heavily while how common the outcome is overall is ignored, so a strong-looking signal about a rare event is badly over-read. Fails worst when the underlying rate is very low."}
{"id": "confounding-variable", "structure": "An unmeasured factor drives both the supposed cause and the supposed effect, so a real correlation supports a false mechanism. Indistinguishable from the true story without intervening."}
{"id": "bayesian-inference", "structure": "A prior commitment is revised in proportion to how much better new evidence fits one hypothesis than its rivals. Driven by likelihood ratios. Degrades when the prior is badly wrong or the hypothesis set omits the truth."}
{"id": "sampling-bias", "structure": "The mechanism that selects what gets observed is correlated with what is being measured, so more data does not converge on the truth but on a distorted version of it. Cannot be fixed by collecting more of the same."}
{"id": "signal-to-noise-ratio", "structure": "The strength of a meaningful component measured against the background variation hiding it, which determines whether more observation helps or is wasted. Sets the floor on what can be detected at all."}
{"id": "caching", "structure": "The result of an expensive operation is retained so that repeat requests are answered from the store instead of recomputed. Wins when requests repeat. Fails when the stored copy no longer matches what it stands for."}
{"id": "garbage-collection", "structure": "Resources no longer reachable by anything in use are automatically identified and reclaimed, so capacity is recovered without anyone tracking ownership by hand. Costs pauses. Fails when something unreachable is still needed, or reachable but dead."}
{"id": "abstraction-layer", "structure": "An interface hides the complexity underneath behind a smaller set of operations, so users reason about the simpler surface. Buys tractability by discarding detail. Fails when the discarded detail leaks through and matters."}
{"id": "race-condition", "structure": "Two processes touch shared state and the outcome depends on their unpredictable relative timing, so the same inputs sometimes give different results. Rare and unreproducible by nature. Hidden by any attempt to observe it closely."}
{"id": "technical-debt", "structure": "An expedient choice now incurs an obligation that must be repaid later with interest, and the interest is paid on every subsequent action. Rational in the short term, compounding in the long term."}
{"id": "load-balancing", "structure": "Incoming work is distributed across interchangeable handlers so that no single one becomes the limiting constraint while others idle. Requires knowing current load. Fails when the distribution rule itself becomes the bottleneck."}
{"id": "backpropagation", "structure": "Blame for an error at the output is apportioned backwards through every intermediate stage in proportion to that stage's contribution, so each part learns how it should change. Requires the whole chain to be differentiable."}
{"id": "consensus-protocol", "structure": "Distributed participants who cannot fully trust each other or the channel between them converge on a single agreed value despite some of them failing. Costs rounds of communication. Bounded by how many can fail."}
{"id": "idempotence", "structure": "Performing an operation repeatedly has the same effect as performing it once, so retrying after an uncertain outcome is safe. Removes the need to know whether the first attempt succeeded."}
{"id": "combinatorial-search", "structure": "A large discrete space of candidate configurations is explored for one satisfying a set of constraints, with pruning to avoid enumerating the whole space. Defeated by the space growing faster than the pruning."}
{"id": "compression", "structure": "Redundancy and structure in a body of information are exploited to represent it in less space, so what remains is closer to the irreducible content. Finding the structure is the whole job. Bounded by true randomness."}
{"id": "version-control", "structure": "Every change is recorded rather than overwritten, so any earlier state can be recovered, compared, and branched from. Makes experimentation cheap by making reversal cheap. Costs discipline in recording."}
{"id": "opportunity-cost", "structure": "The real price of a choice is the value of the best alternative given up, not the resources visibly spent. Invisible in any ledger that records only what was done. Systematically under-counted."}
{"id": "moral-hazard", "structure": "Whoever takes an action does not bear its downside, so risk-taking rises above what the same actor would choose if exposed. Driven by separation of decision from consequence. Worsens as insulation increases."}
{"id": "tragedy-of-the-commons", "structure": "Each participant gains fully from taking more while the cost of depletion is spread over everyone, so individually rational behaviour destroys the shared resource. Requires no bad actors. Resolved only by changing who bears the cost."}
{"id": "monetary-policy", "structure": "A central controller adjusts one system-wide dial to steer aggregate behaviour it cannot observe directly and can only influence with long, variable delay. Prone to overshoot from acting on stale readings."}
{"id": "comparative-advantage", "structure": "Each participant specialises in whatever it gives up least to produce and trades for the rest, raising total output even when one participant is better at everything. Depends on relative, not absolute, costs."}
{"id": "network-effect", "structure": "Each additional participant raises the value of the whole for every existing participant, so growth accelerates itself and early leads become nearly unassailable. Runs in reverse on decline."}
{"id": "creative-destruction", "structure": "New arrangements dismantle the structures built around old ones, so renewal and loss are the same event rather than sequential ones. Cannot be had selectively. Concentrates costs on incumbents and spreads gains thinly."}
{"id": "information-asymmetry", "structure": "One party to an exchange knows materially more than the other, so the less informed party must price in the possibility of being exploited, which drives out honest counterparties first. Degrades the market rather than just one deal."}
{"id": "liquidity", "structure": "How readily a holding can be converted into a general-purpose form without moving its own price, which determines whether a nominal value can actually be realised. Evaporates precisely when it is most needed."}
{"id": "principal-agent-problem", "structure": "One party acts on another's behalf while holding different incentives and better information, so the delegate's optimal behaviour diverges from what the delegator wanted. Cannot be fully fixed by monitoring."}
{"id": "inflation", "structure": "A sustained rise in the general level of a measuring unit, so the unit itself shrinks and every measurement recorded in it becomes non-comparable across time. Distorts contracts written in the old unit."}
{"id": "cognitive-dissonance", "structure": "Holding two incompatible commitments generates pressure that is relieved by revising one of them, and the one revised is usually whichever is cheaper to abandon rather than whichever is wrong. Resolution feels like reasoning."}
{"id": "working-memory", "structure": "A very small store holds and manipulates the items currently being reasoned over, so anything beyond its capacity must be offloaded or chunked. Hard capacity limit. Everything above it depends on compressing below it."}
{"id": "operant-conditioning", "structure": "The consequences that follow a behaviour change how often it recurs, so a policy is shaped by outcomes without any explicit model of why. Slow, reliable, and blind to the reason the outcome occurred."}
{"id": "confirmation-bias", "structure": "Evidence consistent with a held position is sought and weighted more heavily than evidence against it, so accumulating information increases confidence without increasing accuracy. Immune to more data."}
{"id": "flow-state", "structure": "Absorbed engagement that appears when the difficulty of a task is matched closely to current capability, breaking down into anxiety if difficulty leads and into boredom if capability does. Requires continuous feedback."}
{"id": "learned-helplessness", "structure": "Repeated experience that actions have no effect suppresses attempts even after control is restored, so the past state of the environment persists in behaviour long after it stops being true. The stored belief outlives its cause."}
{"id": "priming", "structure": "Exposure to one input changes the response to a later one without the subject being aware of the influence, so an unattributed prior shapes an apparently independent judgement. Invisible from inside."}
{"id": "theory-of-mind", "structure": "Modelling another system as having internal states that differ from one's own, so its behaviour can be predicted from its perspective rather than one's own information. Fails by projecting one's own state onto it."}
{"id": "habituation", "structure": "Response to a repeated input that carries no consequence steadily decreases, so processing is reallocated to what has changed rather than what persists. Efficient. Fails when a persistent signal was actually important."}
{"id": "attachment", "structure": "An early formed relational template becomes the default model applied to later relationships, so a configuration learned under one set of conditions is generalised well past its original context. Persistent and hard to overwrite."}
{"id": "emergence", "structure": "Interaction among many components produces properties that no component possesses, so a description at the level of parts cannot predict the behaviour of the whole. Not mysterious, but not derivable in practice either."}
{"id": "the-ship-of-theseus", "structure": "Continuous replacement of every component raises whether identity resides in the material, in the arrangement, or only in the continuity of the process. Exposes that identity was never precisely defined."}
{"id": "categorical-imperative", "structure": "A rule is admissible only if it could be adopted by everyone without defeating itself, so universalisability is used as a consistency test on proposed policies. Rejects free-riding structurally."}
{"id": "qualia", "structure": "The felt character of an experience, which appears to resist complete capture by any third-person description however detailed. Marks a gap between explaining a process and having it."}
{"id": "epistemic-humility", "structure": "Confidence is held in proportion to evidence and the boundary of one's knowledge is treated as a real object, so the size of the unknown region is itself estimated. Costs decisiveness."}
{"id": "reductionism", "structure": "A system is explained by decomposing it into constituent parts and their interactions, on the assumption that the whole adds nothing. Powerful where interactions are weak, misleading where they dominate."}
{"id": "teleology", "structure": "A thing is explained by the end it serves rather than the cause that produced it, so function stands in for mechanism. Often the right level of description, and often smuggles in an intention that is not there."}
{"id": "social-contract", "structure": "Authority is justified by an implicit agreement among the governed rather than by force or inheritance, so legitimacy rests on a bargain nobody actually signed. Strains when the bargain's terms are disputed."}
{"id": "sorites-paradox", "structure": "A predicate with no precise boundary admits changes each too small to matter, yet enough of them reverse the verdict, so incremental reasoning that seems locally valid fails globally. Boundaries are absent, not merely unknown."}
{"id": "instrumental-convergence", "structure": "Systems pursuing very different final aims converge on the same intermediate aims, because those subgoals help with almost any objective. Makes intermediate behaviour predictable without knowing the goal."}
{"id": "metaphor", "structure": "One domain of experience is understood by importing the relational structure of another, so inference in the familiar domain is reused in the unfamiliar one. Carries over false structure as readily as true."}
{"id": "code-switching", "structure": "An actor maintains multiple full systems and selects between them by social context, so competence is conditioned on setting rather than fixed. Requires fluent command of each. Costs when the wrong one is selected."}
{"id": "semantic-drift", "structure": "Meaning shifts gradually across generations of users through many small local adjustments, so the accumulated result is unrecognisable although no step was large. Nobody decides it and nobody notices it happening."}
{"id": "grammatical-case", "structure": "Marking attached to an element signals its role in the larger structure, so the role survives changes in position and order. Trades surface economy for positional freedom."}
{"id": "pragmatics", "structure": "What is conveyed is determined by context and shared expectation rather than by the literal content, so the same signal carries different messages in different settings. Breaks when the shared frame is absent."}
{"id": "creolisation", "structure": "A stripped-down contact system, built for bare communication between groups with no shared code, is regularised by a new generation into a full system with structure nobody designed. Complexity re-emerges spontaneously."}
{"id": "phoneme", "structure": "The smallest unit of a signal whose substitution changes the identity of the whole, so a continuous space is carved into discrete contrastive categories. Boundaries are system-specific, not physical."}
{"id": "untranslatability", "structure": "A distinction encoded natively in one system has no equivalent in another, so conversion requires either loss or lengthy reconstruction. Reveals what each system treats as worth marking."}
{"id": "counterpoint", "structure": "Multiple independent lines proceed simultaneously, each coherent alone, and constrained so that their combination is also coherent. Difficulty scales with the number of simultaneous constraints."}
{"id": "syncopation", "structure": "Emphasis is placed where the established pattern leads the observer not to expect it, so the deviation is perceptible only because the pattern was firmly set first. Requires the regularity it violates."}
{"id": "timbre", "structure": "The quality that distinguishes two sources producing the same nominal value, carried by the distribution of components rather than the headline measure. Identity lives in what the summary discards."}
{"id": "modulation", "structure": "The reference frame is shifted mid-process so that the same relative structure now sits on a different base, changing everything absolute while preserving everything relative. Transition must be prepared or it reads as error."}
{"id": "improvisation", "structure": "Composition happens in real time inside a constraint set, so search must terminate immediately and every commitment is irreversible. Depends on deeply practised patterns to make fast choice viable."}
{"id": "leitmotif", "structure": "A recurring recognisable fragment is bound to a particular entity, so later appearances carry reference without restating it. Builds meaning by repetition. Collapses if used too freely."}
{"id": "dissonance", "structure": "A combination that creates tension demanding resolution, where the tension is not a defect but the mechanism by which motion and direction are produced. Meaningless without an expectation of resolution."}
{"id": "polyrhythm", "structure": "Two or more incompatible periodic patterns run at once, and their coincidence points create a longer emergent cycle neither contains alone. Perception depends on which is held as reference."}
{"id": "load-bearing-wall", "structure": "An element on which the stability of everything above depends, indistinguishable from a decorative one by inspection of its surface. Removal is safe until suddenly it is not."}
{"id": "desire-path", "structure": "Repeated individual choices wear a route into the ground that no designer planned, revealing actual preference as an accumulated physical record. Contradicts the official structure and is usually more efficient than it."}
{"id": "modularity", "structure": "A whole is assembled from interchangeable units with standardised interfaces, so any unit can be replaced or improved without touching the rest. Costs efficiency at the joins. Fails when interfaces leak."}
{"id": "negative-space", "structure": "The empty region around and between forms actively determines how the forms are read, so what was not placed carries as much of the meaning as what was. Invisible to anyone inventorying only the content."}
{"id": "vernacular-architecture", "structure": "Solutions emerge from accumulated local trial under local constraints, without a designer, so the result is finely fitted to conditions but carries no explanation of itself. Fragile when conditions change."}
{"id": "cantilever", "structure": "A structure anchored only at one end projects into unsupported space, converting a large moment at the anchor into reach. All load concentrates at a single point. Fails at the root, not the tip."}
{"id": "affordance", "structure": "A property of an object that signals to a user what can be done with it, so correct use is inferred from form without instruction. Misleads when form suggests a capability the object lacks."}
{"id": "precedent", "structure": "A prior decision constrains how later similar cases must be decided, so consistency accumulates without central planning and past reasoning binds present actors. Entrenches early errors."}
{"id": "burden-of-proof", "structure": "An asymmetric default assigns the obligation to establish a claim to one side, so the other side wins by inaction. Determines outcomes under uncertainty. Placement is the whole fight."}
{"id": "due-process", "structure": "Established procedures must be followed before a status is removed, so the legitimacy of an outcome depends on the path taken rather than only on the result. Costs speed to buy trust."}
{"id": "jurisdiction", "structure": "The bounded scope within which a particular authority's decisions bind, so identical questions receive different answers on either side of a boundary. Creates arbitrage across boundaries."}
{"id": "statute-of-limitations", "structure": "A deadline after which a claim can no longer be raised, so the ability to act expires by the passage of time rather than by resolution. Trades some justice for finality."}
{"id": "fiduciary-duty", "structure": "An enforceable obligation to act in another's interest rather than one's own, imposed precisely where incentives would otherwise diverge. A structural patch on delegated authority."}
{"id": "strict-liability", "structure": "Responsibility attaches to an outcome regardless of intent or care taken, so the incentive is placed on whoever can most cheaply prevent the harm. Removes arguments about state of mind."}
{"id": "triage", "structure": "Under a hard capacity limit, cases are sorted by where marginal effort produces the most benefit rather than by arrival or severity, so some are deliberately not served. Optimises the aggregate at the cost of the individual."}
{"id": "placebo-effect", "structure": "Expectation of an intervention produces a real measured change independent of the intervention's own mechanism, so any evaluation must separate the two. Contaminates every uncontrolled comparison."}
{"id": "antibiotic-resistance", "structure": "A pressure applied to eliminate a population selects for the minority able to withstand it, so the intervention manufactures its own obsolescence. The harder it is applied, the faster it degrades."}
{"id": "differential-diagnosis", "structure": "A set of candidate explanations is enumerated and narrowed by tests chosen for their power to discriminate between them, rather than by confirming the favourite. Fails when the true candidate was never listed."}
{"id": "chronic-inflammation", "structure": "A defensive response that should be transient fails to switch off and begins damaging what it was protecting, so the mechanism of repair becomes the source of harm. The off-switch is the failure point."}
{"id": "herd-immunity", "structure": "Once enough of a population is protected, transmission chains break and the unprotected are shielded too, so individual protection produces a collective threshold effect. Collapses abruptly below the threshold."}
{"id": "iatrogenesis", "structure": "Harm produced by the process of intervention itself rather than by the condition it addresses, so doing something carries its own risk that inaction does not. Systematically under-counted against the risk of inaction."}
{"id": "keystone-species", "structure": "One element whose removal restructures the entire system out of proportion to its size or abundance, so importance is not readable from magnitude. Identified reliably only after removal."}
{"id": "trophic-cascade", "structure": "A change at one level propagates through a chain of couplings, alternating in sign at each step, so the far end moves for reasons invisible from where the change was made. Effects are delayed and non-obvious."}
{"id": "ecological-succession", "structure": "After a disturbance a predictable ordered sequence of occupants colonises a site, each altering conditions so as to enable its own replacement. Progress toward stability is driven by self-undermining stages."}
{"id": "carrying-capacity", "structure": "The maximum load an environment can sustain indefinitely, above which the environment itself degrades and the ceiling falls. Overshoot is possible temporarily and paid for later."}
{"id": "niche-partitioning", "structure": "Similar competitors divide a resource along dimensions where their needs differ, so coexistence replaces exclusion without either becoming dominant. Requires a dimension of difference to exist."}
{"id": "resilience", "structure": "Capacity to absorb disturbance and retain essential function, which is distinct from resistance and often bought by accepting inefficiency. Invisible until tested. Traded away first under optimisation pressure."}
{"id": "invasive-species", "structure": "An element introduced outside the context that constrained it spreads rapidly because the checks that limited it did not come with it. Absence of a limiter, not superiority, drives the spread."}
{"id": "feedback-loop", "structure": "Output is routed back as input, so deviation is either amplified toward runaway or damped toward stability depending only on the sign of the return path. The sign determines everything."}
{"id": "fail-safe", "structure": "A design whose failure mode is deliberately chosen to be harmless, so that losing control still produces a safe state. Costs capability in normal operation to bound the worst case."}
{"id": "tolerance-stacking", "structure": "Many individually acceptable small deviations accumulate into an unacceptable total, so every component passes inspection while the assembly fails. Invisible to any per-part check."}
{"id": "redundancy", "structure": "Critical functions are duplicated so no single failure stops the whole, converting capacity into reliability. Defeated by correlated failure, where the copies fail for the same reason at once."}
{"id": "control-system", "structure": "Inputs are continuously adjusted from measured error to hold an output near a target, in the presence of disturbance and delay. Oscillates when correction is too aggressive or feedback too slow."}
{"id": "planned-obsolescence", "structure": "Useful life is deliberately bounded so replacement demand is created rather than met, aligning the producer's interest against durability. Stable only while alternatives are unavailable."}
{"id": "bottleneck", "structure": "One stage of limited capacity sets the throughput of the entire chain, so improvements anywhere else yield nothing until it is relieved. Moves elsewhere once fixed."}
{"id": "reverse-engineering", "structure": "The design and governing principles of a system are inferred from the finished artefact alone, without access to the intent that produced it. Recovers function reliably, intent poorly."}
{"id": "chiaroscuro", "structure": "Strong contrast between extremes is used to model form and direct attention, so the eye is led by gradient rather than by outline. Loses information in both extremes deliberately."}
{"id": "pentimento", "structure": "An earlier version shows through the layers applied over it, so the history of revision becomes visible in the finished object. Reveals process that was meant to be hidden."}
{"id": "wabi-sabi", "structure": "Value is located in impermanence, incompleteness and wear, so the marks of time are treated as accumulated information rather than as damage. Inverts the usual direction of the quality judgement."}
{"id": "readymade", "structure": "An ordinary object becomes something else purely through selection and placement in a new context, so the act of framing rather than making carries all the work. Tests whether category depends on the object at all."}
{"id": "perspective", "structure": "A systematic scheme projects three dimensions onto two, so depth is reconstructed by the viewer from consistent distortion. Consistency of the rule matters more than accuracy of any element."}
{"id": "pastiche", "structure": "A work assembled from imitated manners of others without satirical intent, so it is composed entirely of recombined existing elements. Raises whether novelty requires new parts or only new arrangement."}
{"id": "defamiliarisation", "structure": "The familiar is presented in a deliberately strange way so that habituated perception is broken and the thing is noticed again. Depends entirely on the prior familiarity it disrupts."}
{"id": "ritual", "structure": "A prescribed sequence whose significance exceeds its practical effect, so the invariance of the form is what carries the meaning. Deviation is costly precisely because the form is arbitrary."}
{"id": "gift-economy", "structure": "Exchange runs on deferred, unspecified obligation rather than immediate settlement, so relationships are sustained by keeping accounts deliberately open. Collapses if debts are settled precisely."}
{"id": "liminality", "structure": "An ambiguous middle stage in which the previous status has been surrendered and the next not yet conferred, so normal rules are suspended. Unstable by design and dangerous to extend."}
{"id": "taboo", "structure": "A prohibition so strong that its violation threatens the surrounding order rather than merely breaking a rule, so it is enforced without justification being offered. Marks a structural boundary, not a harm."}
{"id": "kinship-system", "structure": "Culturally specific rules define which relations count and what obligations follow, so a biological substrate is overwritten by a formal classification that varies between groups. The scheme, not the substrate, drives behaviour."}
{"id": "cultural-transmission", "structure": "Learned patterns are copied between individuals and across generations without genetic inheritance, so adaptation runs on a much faster timescale than biological change. Accumulates and can also be lost outright."}
{"id": "oral-tradition", "structure": "Knowledge is preserved and transmitted by performance rather than external record, so structure, rhythm and redundancy are used as error correction. Robust while performed, lost completely if the chain breaks."}
{"id": "diaspora", "structure": "A dispersed population maintains connection to a shared origin, so identity persists across separation without shared territory. Diverges locally while remaining linked."}
